# Used only by `npm run build:hospital` (see package.json — runs
# `vite build --mode hospital`, which makes Vite load THIS file instead of
# .env). This produces a separate build for the hospital's local machine,
# pointed at the LOCAL Laravel backend instead of the cloud one — the
# Vercel build and this build are two different artifacts from the same
# codebase, not one build shared by both deployments (see .env.example for
# why: VITE_API_BASE_URL is baked in at build time, a browser can't switch
# it later).
#
# EDIT THIS before running build:hospital: point it at wherever the local
# backend actually runs on the hospital's network — e.g. http://localhost/api
# if this frontend build is served from the same machine as the local
# Laravel server, or http://<local-server-ip>/api if served separately.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost/api
